[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Software Requirements Specification - Operating Scenarios
UID: DOC-SSS003
VERSION: 1.0.0
OPTIONS:
  MARKUP: Text

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-NBK-007
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Charge scenarios
STATEMENT: >>>
Required charge scenarios: constant-current, constant-power, constant-voltage,
charge tapering, partial charge, charge termination, overcharge protection,
low-temperature charging, high-temperature charging, charging with hydrogen
evolution, and charging with limited electrolyte circulation.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Each listed scenario has a unique IA-SCN-CHG-* ID, Python scenario function, notebook,
and seaborn plots.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-NBK-008
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Discharge scenarios
STATEMENT: >>>
Required discharge scenarios: constant-current, constant-power, variable-load,
partial discharge, deep discharge, oxygen-limited, thermal-limited, high-rate,
low-rate, and 100-hour discharge.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Each listed scenario has a unique IA-SCN-DCH-* ID, Python scenario function, and notebook.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-NBK-009
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Transition scenarios
STATEMENT: >>>
Required transition scenarios: charge to discharge, discharge to charge, rapid power
reversal, rest period, voltage relaxation, repeated cycling, startup, shutdown, and
restart after protection trip.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Each listed scenario has a unique IA-SCN-TRN-* ID, Python scenario function, and notebook.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-NBK-010
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Chemistry scenarios
STATEMENT: >>>
Required chemistry scenarios: iron passivation, magnetite formation, hydrogen evolution,
oxygen starvation, carbonate accumulation, water depletion, electrolyte dilution,
electrolyte concentration increase, electrode aging, and catalyst degradation.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Each listed scenario has a unique IA-SCN-CHM-* ID, Python scenario function, and notebook.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-NBK-011
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Environmental scenarios
STATEMENT: >>>
Required environmental scenarios: cold start, hot start, ambient temperature cycling,
high relative humidity, low relative humidity, high altitude, reduced atmospheric
oxygen, and thermal control failure.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Each listed scenario has a unique IA-SCN-ENV-* ID, Python scenario function, and notebook.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-NBK-012
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Mechanical fault scenarios
STATEMENT: >>>
Required mechanical fault scenarios: fan failure, pump failure, filter blockage,
valve failure, electrolyte leak, reservoir depletion, reduced circulation, heat
exchanger failure, and ventilation failure.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Each listed scenario has a unique IA-SCN-MCH-* ID, Python scenario function, and notebook.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-NBK-013
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Electrical scenarios
STATEMENT: >>>
Required electrical scenarios: cell short, cell open circuit, cell imbalance, stack
mismatch, converter overload, DC bus undervoltage, DC bus overvoltage, inverter
current limit, and sensor failure.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Each listed scenario has a unique IA-SCN-ELC-* ID, Python scenario function, and notebook.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-NBK-014
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Grid scenarios
STATEMENT: >>>
Required grid scenarios: voltage sag, voltage swell, underfrequency, overfrequency,
frequency-watt response, volt-var response, grid disconnection, reconnection,
ride-through, and active/reactive power limits.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Each listed scenario has a unique IA-SCN-GRD-* ID, Python scenario function, and notebook.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-NBK-015
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Long-term scenarios
STATEMENT: >>>
Required long-term scenarios: 100-hour discharge, multiple-day energy dispatch,
charge/discharge cycling, seasonal storage, calendar aging, cycle aging, capacity
fade, efficiency degradation, and annual operating profile.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Each listed scenario has a unique IA-SCN-LT-* ID, Python scenario function, and notebook.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-NBK-016
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Characterization scenarios
STATEMENT: >>>
Required characterization scenarios: current-voltage polarization curves,
charge/discharge voltage versus SOC, efficiency versus power, efficiency versus
temperature, SOC versus time, oxygen demand versus power, hydrogen generation versus
charge current, KOH concentration sweep, thermal response, parameter sensitivity,
and uncertainty analysis.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Each listed scenario has a unique IA-SCN-CHR-* ID, Python scenario function, and notebook.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SCN-CHG-CC
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Constant-current charging
STATEMENT: >>>
Apply a constant charging current and record voltage, SOC, HER, and temperature.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
SOC increases. Terminal voltage rises. Current remains at the commanded charge value
until a termination limit.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-NBK-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SCN-CHG-CP
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Constant-power charging
STATEMENT: >>>
Apply a constant charging power command.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Electrical power tracks the charge setpoint within solver tolerance until limits.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-NBK-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SCN-CHG-CV
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Constant-voltage charging
STATEMENT: >>>
Hold a constant charge voltage after a current-limited approach.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Charge current tapers as SOC increases under CV hold.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-NBK-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SCN-CHG-TAPER
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Charge tapering
STATEMENT: >>>
Execute CC-CV tapering to a cutoff current.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Simulation stops or flags complete when abs(I) falls below cutoff while voltage is held.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-NBK-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SCN-CHG-PARTIAL
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Partial charge
STATEMENT: >>>
Charge from an intermediate SOC to a higher intermediate SOC.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Final SOC is between the start SOC and 1.0 and matches the scheduled stop.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-NBK-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SCN-CHG-TERM
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Charge termination
STATEMENT: >>>
Terminate charge on voltage, current, SOC, or hydrogen-rate limits.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Supervisory controller enters a rest or protection mode when a documented limit is crossed.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-NBK-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SCN-CHG-OVER
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Overcharge protection
STATEMENT: >>>
Attempt overcharge and verify protection action.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Current is removed or limited after the overcharge threshold. HER may rise before trip.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-NBK-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SCN-CHG-LOWT
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Low-temperature charging
STATEMENT: >>>
Charge at a cold ambient temperature within the property-model domain.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Polarization is larger than the 298 K reference case. Solver remains stable.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-NBK-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SCN-CHG-HIGHT
STATUS: Active
TITLE: High-temperature charging
STATEMENT: >>>
Charge at an elevated ambient temperature within the property-model domain.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
HER rate is higher than the 298 K reference at the same current.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-NBK-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SCN-CHG-HER
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Charging with hydrogen evolution
STATEMENT: >>>
Charge under conditions that produce measurable HER.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
H2 inventory increases. Faradaic efficiency of iron conversion is less than 1.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-NBK-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SCN-CHG-LOWFLOW
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Charging with limited electrolyte circulation
STATEMENT: >>>
Charge with reduced or zero electrolyte pump flow.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Local concentration gradients or voltage penalty exceed the circulating reference case.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-NBK-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SCN-DCH-CC
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Constant-current discharge
STATEMENT: >>>
Apply a constant discharge current.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
SOC decreases. Voltage falls. Iron inventory is oxidized.
<<<
