- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-NBK-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SCN-TRN-REVERSAL
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Rapid power reversal
STATEMENT: >>>
Reverse power on a short time scale relative to thermal states.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Electrical states respond faster than thermal states. Solver remains stable.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-NBK-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SCN-TRN-REST
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Rest period
STATEMENT: >>>
Hold zero applied current after operation.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Terminal current is ~0. Voltage relaxes toward equilibrium.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-NBK-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SCN-TRN-RELAX
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Voltage relaxation
STATEMENT: >>>
Record open-circuit voltage relaxation after current interruption.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The absolute value of dV/dt decreases with time during rest.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-NBK-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SCN-TRN-CYCLE
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Repeated cycling
STATEMENT: >>>
Apply repeated charge/discharge cycles.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
SOC oscillates. Optional degradation states are nondecreasing.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-NBK-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SCN-TRN-STARTUP
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Startup
STATEMENT: >>>
Start auxiliaries and electrical conversion from a rest state.
